# Gate step — data, not code (order 1072-b7eq). Wired by 1087-h2z9.
#
# Triaged from scripts/gate-divergence-declared.txt, where it sat `untriaged`
# since 2026-09-06: present in --ci-full, absent from --check, nobody decided.
# Measured green and cheap on b026372ff (Cheatsheet references), so the honest verdict is to run
# it where every host lands rather than once a day on the release gate.
#
# STEP_SCRIPT is a LITERAL path on purpose (1063-nraf): a binding assembled
# from a variable is invisible to every name-based scan.
STEP_DESC="Checking cheatsheet references resolve"
STEP_SCRIPT="scripts/check-cheatsheet-refs.sh"
STEP_ERROR="a cheatsheet reference does not resolve (1087-h2z9)"
STEP_OK="Cheatsheet references passed"

# Exit 2 from check-cheatsheet-refs.sh means "ripgrep is available neither on
# this host nor in the tillandsias-builder toolbox" — nothing was examined.
# Before this field existed, that tooling gap printed STEP_ERROR and refused the
# land: a content verdict about zero references. Measured on esmeraldinha
# 2026-09-12 (WSL2, no rg), LAND_EXIT=3. Exit 1 remains a genuine unresolved
# reference and still refuses.
STEP_SKIP_EXIT=2
STEP_SKIP_DESC="ripgrep absent on this host and in the tillandsias-builder toolbox"
STEP_SECOND_REGIME="macneo 2026-09-22 darwin ok:rc0-no-verdict-line"
